<!--
    The aggressive preset leaves option `regionedgeorder` (SAILR's ordering of
    the edge the region structurer cuts when no schema applies) at its catalog
    default, off. `auto` selects that preset for every file under 500 KiB, so
    the ordering used to be the default output of small binaries.

    Stage / sub-stage: P8 structure, goto-quality. P0 assertions: `mode
    aggressive`, then `option regionedgeorder on`.

    Source, gcc 11 -O0 x86-64 (after coreutils `ls` set_exit_status), with the
    global's three rip-relative displacements pointed at 0x404000:

        int exit_status;
        void set_exit_status(bool serious)
        {
          if (serious)
            exit_status = 2;
          else if (exit_status == 0)
            exit_status = 1;
        }

    The ordering cuts the edge from the `exit_status == 0` test into the
    function's exit, which prints as a guard return. The catalog defaults and
    `mode aggressive` print the source's `else if`; `option regionedgeorder on`
    prints the inner test as `if (dat_404000) return;`, as `mode aggressive`
    did while it carried the option.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x401000" readonly="true">
554889e589f88845fc807dfc00740cc705e72f000002000000eb148b05df2f000085c0750ac705d12f00000100000090
5dc3
</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x404000">00000000</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x401000" name="set_exit_status"/>
